  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The smallest possible degree of $P-Q$ is $0.$\n\nFor example, suppose $P=-2{x}^{5}$ and $Q=2{x}^{5}+3.$ Then $P+Q=3,$ which is a polynomial of degree $0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
